  "statement": "\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne cylinder has a height of 7 cm and an unknown base radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e. The other has a height of 3 cm and a base radius 2 cm greater than \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnter the formulas for the volumes of the two cylinders in your calculator. Find the value of \u003ci\u003er \u003c/i\u003efor which the two volumes are equal, to the nearest tenth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class\u003d\"problemstatement_figure\"\u003e\n \u003cimg src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/f-80-6-q.gif\"\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
  "statementFigure": null,
  "question": null,
  "widgetSlot": null,
  "steps": [
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the formula for the volume of a cylinder with height 7 cm and base radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe formula for the volume of a cylinder with height 7 cm and base radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e is\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003cimg width\u003d\"71\" height\u003d\"25\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/image008.gif\" class\u003d\"text-top\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFind the formula for the volume of a cylinder with height 3 cm and base radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e + 2.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe formula for the volume of a cylinder with height 3 cm and base radius \u003ci\u003er\u003c/i\u003e + 2 cm is\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003cimg width\u003d\"105\" height\u003d\"25\" src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/image009.gif\" class\u003d\"text-top\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eEnter the two functions into your calculator.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eEnter the two functions into your calculator.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20188\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qyeq.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20188\u0026quot;,265)\"\u003e. For Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e, key in \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20189\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q7.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20190\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003eΠ \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20191\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qx73.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20191\u0026quot;,263)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20192\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qxsqr.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20192\u0026quot;,260)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20193\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20193\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e. For Y\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e, key in \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20194\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q3.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20195\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20196\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qpi.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20196\u0026quot;,200)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20197\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qopenparen.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20197\u0026quot;,196)\"\u003e\u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20198\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qx73.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20198\u0026quot;,263)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20199\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qplus.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20199\u0026quot;,203)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20200\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20201\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qcloseparen.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20201\u0026quot;,121)\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20202\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qxsqr.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20202\u0026quot;,260)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-5 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/f-80-6-1.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eIt\u0027s probably easier to use a table than a graph.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eIt\u0027s probably easier to use a table than a graph.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20203\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20204\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtblset.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20204\u0026quot;,231)\"\u003e and make sure TblStart \u003d 1 and Δ Tbl \u003d 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20205\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20206\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtable.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20206\u0026quot;,228)\"\u003e to view the table.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eFor \u003ci\u003ex\u003c/i\u003e \u003d 1, 2, and 3, you\u0027ll see that Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20207\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/lt.gif\"\u003e Y\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003e. However, for \u003ci\u003ex\u003c/i\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20208\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/gt.gif\"\u003e 4, the numbers in the Y\u003csub\u003e1\u003c/sub\u003e column are greater.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThis means the two volumes are equal for some radius between 3 and 4.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-7 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/f-80-6-2.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eChange the \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20209\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtblset.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20209\u0026quot;,231)\"\u003e values.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20210\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20211\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtblset.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20211\u0026quot;,231)\"\u003e, and change TblStart to 3, and Δ Tbl to 0.1.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-9 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/f-80-6-3.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "hint",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20212\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20213\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtable.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20213\u0026quot;,228)\"\u003e to go back to the table.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20214\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/q2nd.gif\"\u003e \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_20215\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qtable.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_20215\u0026quot;,228)\"\u003e to go back to the table. Scrolling down, we see that the two volumes are very close for the \u003ci\u003ex\u003c/i\u003e–value \u003ci\u003e \u003c/i\u003e3.8.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eSo, the volumes of the two cylinders are equal for a radius of about 3.8 cm.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-11 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_9_1_areasandvolumes_6_80/f-80-6-4.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    }
  ]
